---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE, socialLinks, LEGAL_UPDATED, formatDate } from "../lib/site.mjs";

const social = socialLinks();
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What the Australian Election Tracker collects — almost nothing. No cookies, no analytics, no tracking. How candidate information is handled and how to request a correction."
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This site is deliberately built so that there is very little to collect. It is a
      set of static files. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics, and has no accounts,
      no logins and no tracking scripts of any kind.
    </p>

    <div class="notice" role="note">
      <strong>The short version.</strong> We don't track you. We don't know who you are.
      If you email us, we have your email. If you post a GitHub issue, that's public.
      Candidate records contain only publicly available information about people's
      public candidacies.
    </div>

    <h2 id="not-collected">What we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No cookies are set by this site.</li>
      <li>No analytics, no page-view tracking, no session recording, no heatmaps.</li>
      <li>No advertising networks, no tracking pixels, no third-party scripts.</li>
      <li>No user accounts, logins, newsletters or mailing lists.</li>
      <li>
        No fingerprinting. The site ships no JavaScript bundles at all — the one small
        script it does include only refreshes the election countdown.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="processed">What is processed when you visit</h2>
    <p>
      The site is delivered by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare's servers
      process the technical details of each request — including your IP address, the
      time, the page requested and your browser's user-agent string — in order to serve
      the page and to protect against attacks and abuse. This is standard infrastructure
      logging that we do not control, do not use for analytics and do not combine with
      anything else.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare also enables Network Error Logging on the sites it serves. If your
      browser fails to load a page, it may send a technical error report to Cloudflare's
      reporting endpoint. Successful requests are not reported. This is a hosting-level
      feature rather than anything this site does, and it is not analytics — but it is a
      report leaving your browser, so it is listed here for completeness.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Cloudflare acts as our hosting provider. See
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="nofollow noopener">
        Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="you-contact">If you contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Email sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> reaches a private
      mailbox. We keep correspondence for as long as needed to deal with the matter and
      to keep a record of corrections. We do not add you to any list, and we do not pass
      your details to anyone else.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you raise a correction through <a href={SITE.issues}>GitHub Issues</a>, be aware
      that issues are <strong>public</strong> and governed by GitHub's own terms and
      privacy policy. If your request involves anything you would rather not publish,
      email instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      We never publish the identity or contact details of anyone who submits information
      to us.
    </p>

    <h2 id="social">Our social accounts</h2>
    <p>
      The project maintains only the accounts listed below (Election Tracker brand).
      Personal or unrelated channels are not part of this site. See the repository
      document <code>docs/SOCIAL.md</code> for the brand split.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {
        social.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <a href={s.url} rel="nofollow noopener">
              {s.label}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you interact with those platforms, the platform collects information about you
      under its own policies, which we neither control nor receive in bulk. Nothing on
      this website loads third-party social embeds, like buttons, or tracking pixels.
    </p>

    <h2 id="candidates">Information about candidates and members</h2>
    <p>
      This site records information about people acting in a public political capacity:
      candidates who have publicly announced or been endorsed, and sitting members of
      parliament. Every record is drawn from a published, cited source.
    </p>
    <p>We deliberately limit what is recorded:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>What we publish:</strong> name, the party and seat associated with the
        candidacy, its status, the dates of any change, and the sources supporting each.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What we never publish:</strong> home addresses, contact details, family
        details, employment unrelated to the candidacy, or any personal information the
        person has not themselves made public in the context of standing for office.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What we never record at all:</strong> rumour, speculation or unverified
        allegations.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Full detail is in the <a href="/methodology">methodology</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="corrections">Corrections, and asking us to remove something</h2>
    <p>
      If a record about you is wrong, out of date, or should not be there, tell us and we
      will deal with it promptly. Requests concerning living people are prioritised above
      all other work on this project.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because the dataset is a public Git repository, corrections are made by adding a
      new entry rather than silently erasing history — the correction and its reason
      remain visible. If you believe information should be removed entirely rather than
      corrected, say so and explain why, and we will consider it on the merits.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also ask what information we hold about you.
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="handling">How we handle information generally</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to handle personal information consistently with the Australian Privacy
      Principles in the <i>Privacy Act 1988</i> (Cth): collect only what is needed, keep
      it accurate, keep it secure, and correct it when asked. No credentials, private
      correspondence or unpublished submissions are ever committed to the public
      repository.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are unhappy with how we have handled a privacy matter, contact us first. If
      you remain dissatisfied, you may complain to the
      <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="nofollow noopener">
        Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a public-interest reference work not directed at children, and it
      collects nothing from anyone, including children.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes materially, the date below changes with it. Because the site
      is published from a public repository, every past version of this page and the
      exact date it changed can be inspected in the
      <a href={SITE.repo}>commit history</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="updated muted">Last reviewed {formatDate(LEGAL_UPDATED)}.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  ul strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .notice {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .updated {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
